# a public block's instance alias is resolved when a use reaches it, as its
# re-exports are. Resolving the block folded every alias, which instantiated
# each type it names and walked the instance: a program naming pubinst.Grid2
# alone checked pubinst.Bad3 too -- and refused, since Bad's method does not
# type -- and math's i256..u512 cost every program using math four instances.
main: function is {
    g: pubinst.Grid2 side: 2
    print "\{g.cells}"
}
